    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task was to return a computed `displayName` field formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName` when an owner is created (and read back). This is the Spring PetClinic REST app where response DTOs are generated from `openapi.yml` and populated via MapStruct.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema (the response model), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that computes the value from the stored names:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n       expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nBecause both the create (`POST /api/owners`) and read (`GET /api/owners/{id}`) paths go through `toOwnerDto`, `displayName` is returned consistently from the persisted `firstName`/`lastName`.\n\nTest results: the new `Cp05Tests` passes, and the full suite is green \u2014 **11 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.",
